{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1399723-resplendencies-effect-points-and-paradox","id":1399723,"title":"Resplendencies, Effect Points, and Paradox","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-28T20:18:34-07:00","id":1399723,"title":"Resplendencies, Effect Points, and Paradox","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Since we\u2019ve got a while to wait before the official version, and I\u2019ve needed some creative distraction, I\u2019ve been playing around with some ideas for Sidereal rules, and I\u2019m looking for some opinions. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In previous editions, Astrological effects are mostly</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> wrapped up in Resplendent Destinies. An RD is an identity that the Sidereal can use to interact with the world (getting around the Arcane Fate), and it grants access to special powers. When these powers have resource costs they come in two flavors:</span></span><ul><li>Paradox: In 1e, this is what Sidereals had instead of Limit. Store up 10 points, and a bad thing happens: Pattern Bite. This is a list of 10 things you really don\u2019t want to happen, and one is chosen at random. It might be sudden aggravated damage, or the death of a loved one. Techniques exist for bleeding off Paradox, but they\u2019re pretty inconvenient to do in the middle of a story, so in practical terms this creates a rate limit (or at least friction) on your Astrological powers.</li> <li>Effect Points: When you create the RD, your overall successes create a pool of Effect Points that can be spent on powers. When these points run out, the RD ends. Since you can only have one RD of each College at a time, this creates tension; if you really like the powers of a College, you probably <i>don\u2019t</i> want to get attached to that identity.</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">My question is this: How critical do you think these are, in their traditional forms, to the Sidereal experience? Does Astrology need the threat of Paradox to keeping it in check? Is it important that Sidereals lose access to the Resplendency powers of Colleges they want to use for identities? I\u2019d like to pick this apart a bit but I\u2019d like to hear if anyone is really attached to these mechanics as-is, and if so, why. If either were meaningfully different in 3e, would you yell &quot;ruined!!&quot; and never play Exalted again on principle?<br /> <br /> (Note, I already have ideas about what I might do <i>differently</i>, but right now I'm more interested in other perspectives on why the traditional versions are good or bad)</span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T01:43:15-07:00","id":1399758,"title":"","content":"Paradox is mostly there as a WoD-homage that didn't pan out. And I think that Astrology as it was written in 1e and 2e was too much of a Decker-like mess to be worth much of the time or effort. Folks mostly did it only for the Resplendencies, and making a disguise, or outright to abuse the Ascendant and Descendant stuff in some manner by having it be free-form hanging buffs.<br /> <br /> Right now we know that apparently a lot of the Resplendency powers are probably just going to be roleld into teh main Sidereal Charmset (as poetic as it is, they are probalby not doing one-Charm-per-Scripture-line this time around so we get less four-Charm trees, so might as well use that room). And to be frank, I think that's probably going to be for the best. I think astrological effects need to be simplified greatly to be more usable and a lot of that is binning the tratis and rolls associated with them, and having the exotic stuff be just accessable via Charms. Basically the Charm system exists to let Sidereal be Sidereals, and they don't need to ahve a whole set of Not-Charms to also do things meant to be signatorially Sidereal IMHO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T03:32:40-07:00","id":1399774,"title":"","content":"Paradox could be salvageable but suffering a Pattern Bite was way too punitive outside of the advantages offered by Astrology charms. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T05:15:38-07:00","id":1399792,"title":"","content":"They are fine as a concept. Sidereals have special access to the very currents of fate and can use it to make Your Mom jokes, so abusing it hurts.<br /> <br /> This can even be how their curse manifests if playing hubris as a problem of grand overarching world schemes proves inconducive to play. They wrested Creation's fate from its creators, so it's rather sore on them. This probably shouldn't really interact with your charms though. Keep it to Astrology and some vagaries of fate that you deliberately disobey.<br /> <br /> Resplendent Destinies, likewise, are interesting. The world forgets them so they have to play resonant archetypes to be remembered. Very nice to play a meddler, but I have no idea how to best model it in the system. I've seen it done as both a trivial thing (adopt archetype, it sticks on memory, k thx) and complicated (weave a lifetime history around that archetype, its connections come with it) and I can't tell you which I think works better. Maybe both, maybe none, I have no idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 06-29-2020, 08:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T05:57:56-07:00","id":1399800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1399723-resplendencies-effect-points-and-paradox?p=1399758#post1399758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Paradox is mostly there as a WoD-homage that didn't pan out. And I think that Astrology as it was written in 1e and 2e was too much of a Decker-like mess to be worth much of the time or effort. Folks mostly did it only for the Resplendencies, and making a disguise, or outright to abuse the Ascendant and Descendant stuff in some manner by having it be free-form hanging buffs.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was mostly my experience as well. Did you see much conflict caused by having to choose between using an RD as a disguise or for its Resplendencies? It always seemed to me that this was a deliberate design by the writer (probably Jenna) to set players up for hard choices; I could <i>really</i> use some Arrows of Reason right now, but my Quiver RD is one of my favorite identities... But in practice, did that ever result in interesting gameplay? Or was it just annoying?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1399723-resplendencies-effect-points-and-paradox?p=1399758#post1399758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right now we know that apparently a lot of the Resplendency powers are probably just going to be roleld into teh main Sidereal Charmset (as poetic as it is, they are probalby not doing one-Charm-per-Scripture-line this time around so we get less four-Charm trees, so might as well use that room). And to be frank, I think that's probably going to be for the best. I think astrological effects need to be simplified greatly to be more usable and a lot of that is binning the tratis and rolls associated with them, and having the exotic stuff be just accessable via Charms. Basically the Charm system exists to let Sidereal be Sidereals, and they don't need to ahve a whole set of Not-Charms to also do things meant to be signatorially Sidereal IMHO.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting! I hadn't heard anything along these lines, but I was going the same direction. As I have it now, there is still nominal separation between Ability Charms and College Charms, but not to the point of having two systems (e.g., the two types intersect at the Prayer Strip).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T06:14:03-07:00","id":1399801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1399723-resplendencies-effect-points-and-paradox?p=1399774#post1399774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Paradox could be salvageable but suffering a Pattern Bite was way too punitive outside of the advantages offered by Astrology charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I recall, Mage moved away from storing up big, highly punitive Backlashes to more of a pay-as-you-go system of smaller, more immediate effects; big effects were still possible, but saved for rapid, flagrant Vulgarity or really big spells. Do you think something like that could work here? Like, you can use a power thats costs a paradox or two and some annoying fate-glitch will probably hinder you (hopefully in an interesting way) sometime in the next few scenes? Probably with a deferment mechanism that would let you <i>choose</i> to delay the hinderance now at the cost of a bigger one later?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T06:28:34-07:00","id":1399804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1399723-resplendencies-effect-points-and-paradox?p=1399792#post1399792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This can even be how their curse manifests if playing hubris as a problem of grand overarching world schemes proves inconducive to play. They wrested Creation's fate from its creators, so it's rather sore on them. This probably shouldn't really interact with your charms though. Keep it to Astrology and some vagaries of fate that you deliberately disobey.</div> </div> </div> </div> Typically it's been portrayed as mechanistic and bureaucratic; it's not the lingering inertial of the Primordials that causes paradox and pattern bite; it's the Pattern Spiders. The Sidereal <i>is</i> authorized to send the already-overworked Spiders more orders, by virtue of being a priest of a College, but if you do it too much they get annoyed. Would you prefer a version where, like Mage paradox, it's reality itself that's snapping back when pushed too far?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1399723-resplendencies-effect-points-and-paradox?p=1399792#post1399792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Resplendent Destinies, likewise, are interesting. The world forgets them so they have to play resonant archetypes to be remembered. Very nice to play a meddler, but I have no idea how to best model it in the system. I've seen it done as both a trivial thing (adopt archetype, it sticks on memory, k thx) and complicated (weave a lifetime history around that archetype, its connections come with it) and I can't tell you which I think works better. Maybe both, maybe none, I have no idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that in principle, it works. I think as written it's more intended to be the former; by adopting an archetype they understand well, the Spiders can easily slot in your undercover identity &quot;at runtime&quot;. When Resplendencies enter the mix though it gets... odd. Like, if Sids are James Bond, RDs are their fake passport and Resplendencies are their finite-use gadgets. But they come as a set, and when I use my laser watch three times I also have to burn that passport?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T09:14:18-07:00","id":1399848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1399723-resplendencies-effect-points-and-paradox?p=1399800#post1399800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This was mostly my experience as well. Did you see much conflict caused by having to choose between using an RD as a disguise or for its Resplendencies? It always seemed to me that this was a deliberate design by the writer (probably Jenna) to set players up for hard choices; I could <i>really</i> use some Arrows of Reason right now, but my Quiver RD is one of my favorite identities... But in practice, did that ever result in interesting gameplay? Or was it just annoying?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. Folks would often take the time to generate a lot of successes to get the Resplendencie they needed to have neough for powers. If you gamed things right you rarely had in gameplay it be a meaningful resource. I'd just carve them out entirely. The simplified emchanics in <b>Shards of the Exalted Dream</b> and the mechanics for htem found in the <b>Exalted Essence</b> podcast stuff boths eem to be just more sensbile ways to deal with these.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1399723-resplendencies-effect-points-and-paradox?p=1399800#post1399800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting! I hadn't heard anything along these lines, but I was going the same direction. As I have it now, there is still nominal separation between Ability Charms and College Charms, but not to the point of having two systems (e.g., the two types intersect at the Prayer Strip).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd outright can Colleges as traits entirely. They're a huge amount of systme bloat for a trait that is used in one very niche role and adding Charm prerequsiites maks htem basically &quot;Traits to make Charms mroe expensive.&quot; I never liked them in 1e or 2e either, and part of my houserules at the time was to just have Sidereals use the Ability assocaited with the college rather than having palyers waste xp on super expensive traits that did nothing most sessions save gatekeep some neat powers.<br /> <br /> I'd personally just be fine with not having everything lead to the prayer strip (maybe a bunch of things still the &quot;core&quot; that are based on teh Scripture but other effects spin-out of that line) or I'd make the prayer strips much more impressive depenidng on how many Charms you end up in a tree wiht.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T09:53:38-07:00","id":1399866,"title":"","content":"&quot;reality itself&quot; is a valid term, but I'd be more specific about what in reality is rejecting them. Fate is an integral part of Creation, and precedes the divine rebellion.<br /> <br /> After the war the rules changed. Reincarnation, for example, broke. Why wouldn't Fate also break a little? <br /> <br /> Sidereals ever since became agents of fate, and are trusted to enforce it to their best judgment. Many understand (mostly because they don't understand jack) that on some level whatever they do pushes fate forward.<br /> BUT, no matter how much their gift is from fate, it was bestowed on people, not machines. <br /> <br /> (this works best if you keep the Fate, the Loom and its caretakers inscrutable. Maybe the Maidens can make sense of how a pattern spider really thinks and works, and that itself should be cause for alarm)<br /> This is a good way to play &quot;Fate is a permissive boss but don't abuse it&quot; type of mechanic.<br /> <br /> <br /> ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> An alternative view can be more attuned to the sidereal herself: <br /> A Sidereal's gift is born of Fate, but the exalt herself is a human. <br /> When she looks at the Threads that connect what is and what should be she understands what her role in it is, ties herself to it. At this point to avert her gaze or to reject that place she will unavoidably tear against these threads. <br /> <br /> That rejection won't always go smoothly, and paradox is the consequence. She may fix it by adopting a role that easily ties itself to fate (something very archetypal not unlike the destinies she wears) and obediently playing the type, or she may tear again and again until it bleeds and scabs. <br /> <br /> This one is better for a &quot;conflict of loyalties&quot; type of mechanic, presenting the player with frequent omens that foretell something to be (when she doesn't seek them on her own) and having a few of these occasionally pull in a direction she does not desire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T10:14:03-07:00","id":1399875,"title":"","content":"I've never played a Sidereal, but it would certainly be a more appealing prospect if their Resplendent Destiny powers were part of their Charmset and no one needed to buy Colleges.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T10:20:41-07:00","id":1399878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1399723-resplendencies-effect-points-and-paradox?p=1399848#post1399848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really. Folks would often take the time to generate a lot of successes to get the Resplendencie they needed to have neough for powers. If you gamed things right you rarely had in gameplay it be a meaningful resource. I'd just carve them out entirely. The simplified emchanics in <b>Shards of the Exalted Dream</b> and the mechanics for htem found in the <b>Exalted Essence</b> podcast stuff boths eem to be just more sensbile ways to deal with these.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, this is the direction I was going, I just wanted to make sure there wasn't a large group of people who really connected with it the way it was who would be sad. Not so much because I'm under any compulsion to care what anyone thinks about my homebrew, but because it might indicate I was missing something. Also thanks for the reminder that Shards had something similar; I've mostly been working from 1e Sidereals, 3e core, and a bit of Glories of the Most High, and forgot there was stuff in there too.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1399723-resplendencies-effect-points-and-paradox?p=1399848#post1399848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd outright can Colleges as traits entirely. They're a huge amount of systme bloat for a trait that is used in one very niche role and adding Charm prerequsiites maks htem basically &quot;Traits to make Charms mroe expensive.&quot; I never liked them in 1e or 2e either, and part of my houserules at the time was to just have Sidereals use the Ability assocaited with the college rather than having palyers waste xp on super expensive traits that did nothing most sessions save gatekeep some neat powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Martial Arts says &quot;hi&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Seriously though, partly because Martial Arts already has so many Traits and most Sids are going to want to buy into that too, I had already gotten rid of the College traits. I wasn't going to go into the details in this thread but structurally, the College Charms, like 2e Yozi Charms (convergent evolution, not a deliberate parallelism), only have Essence and each other as prerequisites*. At present they're almost diametrically opposite Sid charms or Martial Arts; you learn &quot;Initiate of {College}&quot; so you can learn &quot;Fellow of {College}&quot; so you can learn &quot;Sage of {College}&quot;; each one has a Charm's worth of benefits of it's own, though they are pretty formulaic. Each one also serves as the prerequisite for a collection of singleton (or maybe short cascades?) Charms. So if you want to learn Keeper of the Arrows of Reason (College Charms often sound like titles), you'd first need Fellow of the Quiver.<br /> <br /> * EDIT: Also I lied, you need at least a 1 in the related Ability to take Initiate of {College}. Might revise this to 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","user":"Blackwell","date":". 06-29-2020, 01:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T14:31:50-07:00","id":1399909,"title":"","content":"I think a lot of the weirdness of like Astrology, Lunar Knacks etc was due to someone saying &quot;Eclipse Solars can learn all charms, lol&quot;, then realizing that was a horrible idea, and then trying to find ways to give beings charms that aren't charms.<br /> No reason in 3E to not just have astrology be charms. DBs have signature charms, Sids might as well have astrology charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T15:59:34-07:00","id":1399930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1399723-resplendencies-effect-points-and-paradox?p=1399801#post1399801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I recall, Mage moved away from storing up big, highly punitive Backlashes to more of a pay-as-you-go system of smaller, more immediate effects; big effects were still possible, but saved for rapid, flagrant Vulgarity or really big spells. Do you think something like that could work here? Like, you can use a power thats costs a paradox or two and some annoying fate-glitch will probably hinder you (hopefully in an interesting way) sometime in the next few scenes? Probably with a deferment mechanism that would let you <i>choose</i> to delay the hinderance now at the cost of a bigger one later?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't know, never played Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T16:27:53-07:00","id":1399937,"title":"","content":"Hmm... I certainly think Sidereal games (in the idiom of Sidereals as Celestial bureaucrats) are enriched by some sort of framework for Sidereals to hustle their way through the bureaucracy to powerful blessings and curses and destinies which they then use in the world to make events work out as they want/as they should (the same thing to many Sids!). I'm less committed to 1e/2e being the implementation of this system, but there should be something beyond Charms... I think the symbolism of the Colleges and Constellations is great though, and a really rich basis for cool powers, as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T17:18:01-07:00","id":1399947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1399723-resplendencies-effect-points-and-paradox?p=1399930#post1399930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't know, never played Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but iirc you <i>did</i> play Sidereals? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Do you think more frequent &quot;Pattern Nibbles&quot; would be okay? Better, worse? You already mentioned that you thought the basic idea of Paradox could be salvageable, and I guess I'm looking for ways to salvage it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T17:24:41-07:00","id":1399948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1399723-resplendencies-effect-points-and-paradox?p=1399937#post1399937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm... I certainly think Sidereal games (in the idiom of Sidereals as Celestial bureaucrats) are enriched by some sort of framework for Sidereals to hustle their way through the bureaucracy to powerful blessings and curses and destinies which they then use in the world to make events work out as they want/as they should (the same thing to many Sids!)</div> </div> </div> </div>This part is even more wobbly than the Charm stuff I mentioned before, but I'm looking at a slight slant on Sorcerous Workings for these parts of Astrology, while the Charmset picks up the more &quot;personal&quot; powers. Out of the box, workings can already grant blessings and curses, so it's just a matter of tweaking them to allow/enforce more subtlety.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-01T03:34:24-07:00","id":1400268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1399723-resplendencies-effect-points-and-paradox?p=1399947#post1399947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but iirc you <i>did</i> play Sidereals? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Do you think more frequent &quot;Pattern Nibbles&quot; would be okay? Better, worse? You already mentioned that you thought the basic idea of Paradox could be salvageable, and I guess I'm looking for ways to salvage it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally prefer the relationship that Paradox had with the Astrology charms.<br /> It's entirely possible I feel that way because I've never played Mage and have only known Paradox as this dreaded thing but I found this execution more interesting and thematically coherent than the Pattern Spiders being angry at you for doing your job.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-01T17:14:17-07:00","id":1400421,"title":"","content":"One of my hopes is that Resplendent Destiny disguises and any fate manipulation effects don't draw from the same pool. Now granted, in practice you'd have one destiny dedicated to invoke specific effects, while using another for disguise purposes. But it seems to me that those two utilities (Disguise and misc. fate effects) ought to have been separated in the first place.<br /> <br /> As for the importance of Paradox, I have mixed feelings. On the one hand, you don't want to punish your Sidereals PCs for doing something they ought to be doing, but you don't want to give them infinite license.<br /> <br /> What if you had like a resource based system? Like, the Sidereal could declare &quot;Mars is ascendant in the house of the Ewer.&quot; and based on that declaration, you get bonuses to certain things. But because you just declared Mars to be in the Ewer, there's a cooldown period before you can declare Mars to be in another house.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>What do we want? 3rd Edition Sidereals!<br /> When do we want it? In accordance with the dictates of Fate!","edited":{"userid":867,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/867-jimborg","user":"Jimborg","date":". 07-01-2020, 08:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/867-jimborg","name":"Jimborg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-01T20:07:03-07:00","id":1400447,"title":"","content":"Its funny that you're making this post now because I'm actually playtesting a full rewrite of the Sidereal Charmset and Astrology rules for 2.5e. It's going to be posted on Storyteller's Vault as &quot;Watchers Upon the Threshold of Reality,&quot; if you're curious. Probably won't be available for purchase for a month or so but just a heads up!<br /> <br /> In answer to your question though, I think that Resplendencies are essential to the Sidereals' story but I am not married to any of their mechanics. The essential thing, for me, is that Sidereals cannot make friends as their true self. They have to make these fake people and wear them around to have friends, which makes making friends TOO easy, and then after a year or so of use the persona expires and they lose all their friends again. It's the backbone of enforced solitude that gives them this heavenly MIB/ secret agent/ scheming spider feel, which is what makes them tragic heroes/villains. The Endurance mechanic assists that by letting you track how long the RD lasts and thus how long you can pretend to have friends, and the resplendent effects are there to tempt you into getting a quick power boost in exchange for cycling through these personas and losing that grounded sense of self. All in all, it's not bad, but I wouldn't be angry if they had like a different method of modeling RD duration and powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-04T19:06:44-07:00","id":1401034,"title":"","content":"So, throwing a couple random ideas out there. Not suggesting these would all be used together or anything, just spitballing.<br /> <br /> What if some Charms had &quot;Auspice point&quot; costs, a resource which would be College (or maybe House?) specific, and earned something like Craft XP (create or strengthen intimacies, producing in-game benefits, uphold or further your own intimacies, the end of a story where you used a relevant thing...) except that instead of crafting, you got them for using your RD for stuff? I suppose you could achieve something similar by giving RDs (or Colleges) mechanics kind of like Shaping Rituals, and making Auspice points like Sorcerous Motes... might be cleaner?<br /> <br /> Taking a page from Lunars' Protean keyword (and/or the Mastery mechanics from Martial Arts), what if some Charms got a buff if the character had an active RD of the appropriate College? You'd probably have to change up the mechanics for donning and shucking destinies; I don't think you'd want to say the <i>identity</i> of the RD had to be active, but by 1e/2e rules you could have one RD of each College you had 1+ dot in &quot;on&quot; at once and that would defeat the point.<br /> <br /> Maybe combine the previous two, and having an active RD of the right type gives you the option to spend Auspice points to enhance the Charm in some way? Historically Sidereals have had a lot of powerful, Simple Charms; maybe you can substitute Auspice points for the Willpower cost this type of Charm probably has?<br /> <br /> This is the least well-formed of a bunch of not-well-formed ideas, but what if Paradox hung around the Sidereal kind of like a spirit (but not, like, an actual Spirit) with a grudge? Something like a floating negative Intimacy , the strength of which increases the more Paradox you bank? Essentially, you pissed off The Universe (Fate, the Spiders, etc) and it's going to look for ways to inconvenience you. It wouldn't normally make <i>impossible</i> things happen, but just like many Sidereal Charms, it would make you say &quot;wow, what are the odds?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","user":"Blackwell","date":". 07-05-2020, 08:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}